 718: ### 48.2 Application to the S30 three-axis fork
 719: 
 720: **Corollary S44.1 (S30 survives the natural window-certificate route)
 721: [PROVEN at the abstract labeled-state scope].** At S30's displayed F
 722: `FirstStone` checkpoint, the three urgent windows through `e=(0,1)` have
 723: pairwise-disjoint hole pairs
 724: 
 725: ```text
 726: {(4,1),(5,1)}, {(0,5),(0,6)}, {(4,-3),(5,-4)}.
 727: ```
 728: 
 729: Thus every nonwinning physical F pair misses at least one window. If the debt
 730: label `E_S={e}` is retained and not physically reconciled, no genuine
 731: nonterminal alleged-winning-`sigma`-consistent shadow pair can carry that
 732: state to a common `Shat FirstStone` node possessing a Definition 39.1
 733: certificate.
 734: 
 735: Even postponing the certificate check until after S's next first placement
 736: does not repair this fixed-debt branch **if** the handler appends one legal
 737: nonwinning `Shat` stone and remains genuine, `sigma`-consistent, and at the
 738: common phase. In the missed S30 window, S's offset-four hole is legal and, by
 739: S30's cross-line check, nonwinning. Filling it leaves `delta_R=1` at common
 740: `SecondStone`, where `m=1`; S39.1 again requires `delta_R>1`, a contradiction.
 741: Before the offset-five terminal move, the handler must therefore physically
 742: reconcile the debt, obtain an actual same-step physical `Shat` stop (which
 743: would refute `sigma`), obtain an earlier sound real-F stop, or leave the
 744: common-phase/Definition-39.1 premises.
 745: 
 746: *Proof.* Pairwise-disjointness gives `tau_E>=3`, while an F turn supplies at
 747: most two physical cells. Apply S44. For the delayed check, use the verified
 748: nonwinning offset-four continuation from S30 and apply S39.1 with `m=1`. QED.
 749: 
 750: **Lemma S45 (exact S30 service transversal) [PROVEN].** At S30's abstract
 751: labeled checkpoint the full urgent family has
 752: 
 753: `tau_E=5`,
 754: 
 755: not merely the inherited lower bound three obtained from the three selected
 756: positive-direction windows.
 757: 
 758: *Proof.* Work axis by axis through `e=(0,1)`. On the Q line `r=1`, real S
 759: occupies q-indices `0,1,2,3`, and no real F stone lies on the line. Of the six
 760: windows through index zero, exactly the starts `-2,-1,0` are urgent. Their
 761: hole-index pairs are
 762: 
 763: `{-2,-1}`, `{-1,4}`, and `{4,5}`.                         (48.1)
 764: 
 765: The first and third pairs are disjoint, so at least two cells are needed;
 766: indices `-1` and `4` hit all three, so the exact Q-axis cost is two.
 767: 
 768: On the R line `q=0`, real S occupies r-indices `1,2,3,4`. Real `F@(0,0)`
 769: blocks every incident candidate except the window with r-start `1`. Its holes
 770: are `(0,5),(0,6)`, so the exact R-axis cost is one.
 771: 
 772: On the QR line `q+r=1`, parameterize by q. Real S occupies q-indices
 773: `-4,0,1,2,3`, and no real F stone lies on this line. The only urgent starts
 774: are again `-2,-1,0`, with the same interval pattern (48.1); its exact cost is
 775: two. The three axis lines meet only at `e`, which is S-owned and belongs to no
