 961:    proves recurring portfolio existence after every adversarial S turn.
 962: 3. **One-debt is not zero-debt.** Immediately after S15 and one straight
 963:    `sigma` pair, a shadow deficit-two window may correspond to a real
 964:    deficit-three window. Requiring debt zero there would make the positive
 965:    class artificially empty at the first relevant checkpoint.
 966: 4. **Terminal readiness is the red line.** Debt one is allowed at shadow
 967:    deficit two but forbidden at deficit one. S42 fails at exactly this
 968:    transition.
 969: 5. **Many-to-one windows are not merged stones.** The portfolio may assign
 970:    several shadow obligations to one real window. No noninjective point map,
 971:    recoloring, or virtual occupancy is inferred.
 972: 6. **The augmented selector has a feasibility test.** At a ready terminal
 973:    state its unique-hole choice is proved legal. At a nonterminal event it
 974:    still needs a service-compatible cell and a next portfolio; no universal
 975:    existence theorem or complete terminal trace is claimed. S49 shows that the
 976:    ready state itself cannot exist at the earliest terminal age.
