 188: ## 65. The maintenance horn: feasibility, reserve cycles, and the readiness cliff
 189: 
 190: ### 65.1 Scalarization of the causal portfolio
 191: 
 192: At a live common pre-query F-role microstep use the inherited families
 193: `U_R^F,U_H^F` and deficits (55.1)--(55.4), and put
 194: 
 195: `mu_R=min{delta_R^F(W):W in U_R^F}`,                         (65.1)
 196: 
 197: `mu_H=min{delta_H^F(V):V in U_H^F}`.                         (65.2)
 198: 
 199: Both minima exist and lie in `{1,...,6}`. The physical position is finite,
 200: there are unblocked far-away windows of deficit six, and liveness excludes
 201: deficit zero. Fix once and for all well-orders of physical windows and legal
 202: coordinates. When a least-deficit real window is needed below, take the first
 203: one in this fixed order. This makes every selection a function of the reached
 204: prefix rather than of an unqueried prescription.
 205: 
 206: **Lemma S55 (scalar CAD feasibility) [PROVEN].** At every such live prefix an
 207: `F-CAD_2^st` portfolio exists exactly when
 208: 
 209: `mu_H>=3`, or `mu_H=2 and mu_R<=3`, or `mu_H=1 and mu_R=1`.   (65.3)
