 211: Moreover, whenever it exists, a causal portfolio is obtained by assigning
 212: every shadow window of deficit at most two to one least real window attaining
 213: `mu_R`.
 214: 
 215: *Proof.* If `mu_H>=3`, the portfolio domain is empty. If `mu_H=2`, every
 216: member of its domain has shadow deficit two. The one-debt inequality permits
 217: a real deficit of at most three, so an assignment exists exactly when
 218: `mu_R<=3`. If `mu_H=1`, terminal readiness applied to a minimum shadow window
 219: requires a real window of deficit at most one. Liveness makes that deficit
 220: exactly one. Conversely, one real deficit-one window can serve every shadow
 221: window of deficit one or two, satisfying readiness for the former and the
 222: one-debt bound for the latter. Many-to-one assignment is expressly permitted
 223: by Definition 55.2. All inputs to the least choice are physical prefix data,
 224: so special-casing these choices and returning `None` elsewhere totalizes one
 225: pre-trace `Option Portfolio` policy exactly as required by section 63. QED.
 226: 
 227: This lemma is only an existence test for the state certificate. It does not
 228: turn the inherited canonical coordinate into a locked coordinate and does not
 229: remove any E-debt service duty.
