 610: the S51 controller problem, not a proof of `NL_F`.
 611: 
 612: ## 67. Ejection coverage: deadline stops and a mirror-clean first-unsafe class
 613: 
 614: ### 67.1 The common-phase deadline stop cover
 615: 
 616: Let `C_CP^S` denote causal common-phase S-role candidate handlers which,
 617: for each observed actual legal real-S append, make exactly one associated
 618: actual legal `Shat` append. Two nonwins preserve the same
 619: `FirstStone`/`SecondStone` phase. A physical `Shat` win is the S51.1
 620: contradiction stop. Such a candidate succeeds at a real-S win only with the
 621: required physical same-coupled-step shadow terminal transfer--P5R when the
 622: winning window meets represented debt, and the restored common-only real-win
 623: duty otherwise. No unmatched F placement or phase-lag escape belongs to this
 624: class.
 625: 
 626: At a real-S pre-placement state let the **S deficit** of an F-unblocked window
 627: be
 628: 
 629: `delta_R^S(W)=6-|W intersect X_S|`.                          (67.1)
 630: 
 631: **Theorem S62 (deadline-deficit stop cover) [PROVEN].** Fix an
 632: alleged-winning `sigma`, a reachable genuine common S/`Shat` microstep, and an
 633: F-unblocked real window `W`. Let `m=2` at `FirstStone` and `m=1` at
 634: `SecondStone`. If
 635: 
 636: `1<=delta_R^S(W)<=m`,                                       (67.2)
 637: 
 638: then every handler in `C_CP^S` meets the following exhaustive, generally
 639: non-disjoint stop cover on a causal legal real-S continuation:
 640: 
 641: 1. an associated `Shat` append wins, which directly contradicts the
 642:    alleged-winning premise and stops under S51.1; or
 643: 2. real S becomes terminal within the remaining `m` placements while the
 644:    associated shadow append is nonterminal, so the applicable physical
 645:    terminal-reflection duty fails.
 646: 
 647: *Proof.* Choose real S's remaining coordinates successively from the holes of
 648: `W`. There are at most `m`. Every chosen hole is legal: `W` already contains
 649: at least four real-S stones, so a hole is at line distance at most two from
 650: one of them. If a real cross-window wins earlier, item 2 is reached earlier
 651: unless the associated shadow append supplies item 1. Otherwise filling the
 652: last hole completes `W`. After each observed real append, inspect the one
 653: physical associated `Shat` append. Its win is item 1 and is never continued.
 654: If none wins, the shadow remains nonterminal when real S completes six, so
 655: the appropriate P5R or common-only terminal-transfer duty fails. QED.
 656: 
 657: This is a stop criterion and negative control, not a live repair. It does not
 658: identify a shadow winning coordinate by itself.
 659: 
 660: **Corollary S62.1 (first-unsafe no-live-repair boundary) [PROVEN].** Let an
 661: observed legal real first placement `S@y` have S52 value `d_y=1`, witnessed by
 662: an F-unblocked window whose post-`y` unique hole is `x`. If the associated
 663: first `Shat` append wins, stop by S51.1. If it is nonterminal, the boards are
 664: at common `SecondStone` and S62 applies with `m=1`. Hence no
 665: `C_CP^S` branch-(A) or branch-(B) response can continue live through this
 666: first-unsafe event: its next response either physically wins for `Shat` or
 667: fails the real-S terminal-reflection duty when real S chooses `x`.
 668: 
 669: The coordinate `y` is an observed choice on the actual candidate-own coupled
 670: history, and `x` is chosen only after that reached prefix. This is not a
 671: free-standing labeled gadget.
 672: 
 673: ### 67.2 Conditional high-transversal handoff
 674: 
 675: **Corollary S62.2 (`tau_E>2` common-handoff barrier) [PROVEN at named handler scope].**
 676: At an actual common F `FirstStone` checkpoint with `tau_E>2`, let a
 677: one-for-one real/shadow F pair be completed without either board becoming
 678: terminal and hand control to a genuine common S/`Shat FirstStone` state. Then
 679: some pre-turn urgent E-window `W` was missed by both real F placements, stays
 680: F-unblocked, and has `delta_R^S(W)<=2`. The next `C_CP^S` turn is covered by
 681: S62.
 682: 
 683: *Proof.* The two real F coordinates form a set of size at most two. Since the
 684: urgent-hole transversal number exceeds two, that set misses the hole set of
 685: some `W in U_E`. Neither append therefore blocks `W`; S-role occupancy did
 686: not change during the F turn, so its deficit remains at most two. Apply S62
 687: at the common handoff. QED.
 688: 
 689: Thus an attempted high-transversal continuation has an exact set of exits:
 690: a sound real-F stop during service; the inherited aligned or misaligned
 691: shadow-terminal event; loss of common-phase membership; a physical `Shat`
 692: contradiction stop on the next turn; or failure of the real-S terminal
 693: transfer. This strengthens S44/S44.1 only for the named actual nonwinning
 694: common-phase handoff. S45's `tau_E=5` S30 position remains an abstract stress
 695: case without candidate-own alleged-winning reachability, and S31's permanent
 696: fence installation remains **OPEN**.
 697: 
 698: ### 67.3 Constructive mirror-clean stop
 699: 
 700: **Definition 67.1 (`A_FU^mc`, mirror-clean first-unsafe stop class).** At a
 701: genuine common-live S/`Shat FirstStone` prefix consistent with a fixed pure
 702: `sigma`, observe a legal real append `S@y` with `d_y=1`. Let `W` witness this
 703: and let `x` be its post-`y` unique hole. For the reached translation/D6
 704: certificate isometry `T`, require
 705: 
 706: - every cell of `W\{y,x}` to have an actual physical
 707:   `Shat@T(c)` on the shadow board; and
 708: - `T(y)` and `T(x)` to be shadow-empty.
 709: 
 710: No `E_S=empty` premise is imposed; unrelated physical debt may remain. The
 711: six cells `T[W]` consist of four `Shat` stones and two holes, so a separate
 712: `Fhat`-unblocked premise would be redundant.
 713: 
 714: **Theorem S63 (mirror-clean first-unsafe terminal stop) [PROVEN].** Every
 715: prefix in `A_FU^mc` has a causal two-step branch-(C) handler. Append the
 716: associated physical `Shat@T(y)`. If it wins, stop immediately. Otherwise,
 717: after any actual legal real second coordinate `r`, append
 718: `Shat@T(x)` on the associated final coupled step. This second shadow append
 719: is legal and completes `T[W]`, independently of `r`. If `S@r` is real
 720: terminal it supplies its physical terminal reflection; if `S@r` is
 721: nonterminal, the `Shat` win directly refutes alleged-winning `sigma`.
 722: 
 723: *Proof.* An isometry maps the engine window `W` to an engine window `T[W]`.
 724: Before the first shadow append it has four physical `Shat` stones and the two
 725: fresh holes `T(y),T(x)`. Either hole lies within line distance at most two of
 726: one of those stones and is therefore shadow-legal. Filling `T(y)` leaves a
 727: five-stone window unless a cross-window has already won. In the nonwinning
 728: case both boards reach `SecondStone`; `T(x)` is still fresh, legal, and the
 729: unique hole of `T[W]`. Its append physically completes six. The inherited S26
 730: terminal-supply and S52 same-coupled-step P5R semantics permit this associated
 731: shadow certificate if the real second append has just terminated, but neither
 732: terminal engine history is continued afterward. QED.
 733: 
 734: There is an important logical boundary. Already at the pre-`y` checkpoint,
 735: `T[W]` is a shadow deficit-two window on `Shat`'s current turn. By the S39
 736: terminal-supply argument and S51.1, an alleged-winning `sigma` cannot actually
 737: survive the two-hole counterplay. Accordingly `A_FU^mc` is a
 738: **direct-refutation stop criterion**, not a nonterminal alleged-winning
 739: continuation class. Its physical nonemptiness is witnessed only against a
 740: legal diagnostic strategy.
 741: 
 742: For that witness, use the folded round-4 `C_shield` terminating extension
 743: immediately before its final real-S pair, with
 744: 
 745: `T(q,r)=(q-2,r)`,
 746: 
 747: `S@(q,1), q=0,1,2,3`, and `Shat@(q,1), q=-2,-1,0,1`.
 748: 
 749: Take `W={(q,1):q=0,...,5}`, `y=(4,1)`, and `x=(5,1)`. Then
 750: `T(y)=(2,1)` and `T(x)=(3,1)` are fresh. The folded extension proves all
 751: prefix legality and no earlier win; its two final coupled placements complete
 752: the real and shadow windows. The unrelated old debt at `(0,5)` remains
 753: physical and shielded, demonstrating why the definition need not assume an
 754: empty debt set. The on-path strategy is not claimed globally winning.
 755: 
 756: The ejection outcome is therefore a genuine positive stop for the
 757: mirror-clean first-unsafe class, an exact no-live-repair theorem for every
 758: other common-phase one-append handler at the same deadline, and a conditional
 759: extension to `tau_E>2` handoffs. Missing/blocked image cells, wrong-role and
 760: unsupported certificates, phase-lag handlers, and arbitrary high-transversal
 761: reconciliation remain **OPEN**.
