 509: For `a in {1,2}`, define the pre-pair adequate real reserve family
 510: 
 511: `A_a(p)={W in U_R^F(p): delta_R^F(W)<=a}`.                 (77.1)
 512: 
 513: If the pair completes live, let `mu_H'` be the exit shadow minimum and set
 514: 
 515: `a'=1 if mu_H'=1, and a'=2 if mu_H'>=2`.                   (77.2)
 516: 
 517: **Theorem S69 (exact S-pair scalar reserve test) [PROVEN].**  Suppose `p`
 518: satisfies `RES_1` and the two S-role pairs complete legally and
 519: nonterminally.  Then:
 520: 
 521: 1. `mu_H' >= mu_H`; shadow-S stones can only block and remove Fhat-unblocked
 522:    windows;
 523: 2. the exit satisfies scalar `RES_1` exactly when
 524: 
 525:    `there exists W in A_{a'}(p) with W intersect Y=empty`;  (77.3)
 526: 
 527: 3. avoidance of `W_*` by both real-S coordinates is sufficient for (77.3);
 528:    and
 529: 4. hitting `W_*` is not by itself a scalar failure: scalar readiness survives
 530:    exactly when another window in `A_{a'}(p)` avoids both real-S cells.
 531: 
 532: *Proof.*  A `Shat` append adds the opposing colour to any Fhat-unblocked
 533: window it meets, removing that window from `U_H^F`; it changes neither Fhat
 534: stones nor deficits of surviving windows.  Thus the shadow minimum cannot
 535: decrease.  The same physical statement on the real board says that the new S
 536: stones remove exactly the old F-unblocked windows meeting `Y`; every
 537: surviving window retains its deficit.  Therefore the exit real minimum is at
 538: most `a'` exactly when (77.3) holds.  By (74.1), that is precisely the real
 539: half required when `mu_H'=1` or `mu_H'>=2`; liveness excludes deficit zero.
 540: 
 541: For item 3, if the entrance has `mu_H>=2`, `RES_1` gives
 542: `delta_R^F(W_*)=mu_R<=2`, and item 1 gives `a'=2`.  If the entrance has
 543: `mu_H=1`, then `mu_R=1`.  When `mu_H'` stays one, `W_*` is adequate for
 544: `a'=1`; when shadow blocking raises the minimum, the same window is adequate
 545: for the relaxed threshold two.  Avoidance keeps it unblocked in all cases.
 546: Item 4 is the exact existence statement (77.3). QED.
 547: 
 548: The theorem gives a useful joint classification.  If shadow S leaves a
 549: deficit-one Fhat window alive, real S must leave some real deficit-one window
 550: alive.  If shadow S blocks every such shadow window and raises `mu_H'` to at
 551: least two, real S need retain only a deficit-at-most-two reserve.  Shadow
 552: blocking is therefore scalar-neutral or helpful; real S is the only role
 553: which can destroy the real reserve family.
