1087: ### 81.3 Terminal and stop grammar
1088: 
1089: For detached reading, the valid stop semantics are:
1090: 
1091: - real F wins before `sigma`: sound real stop; do not continue it;
1092: - paired real-F/`Fhat` wins in one section-53 event: sound co-terminal stop;
1093: - `Shat` wins on a legal candidate-own counterplay: direct contradiction to
1094:   alleged winning; do not continue it;
1095: - real S wins: require physical P5R for a debt-meeting win or the distinct
1096:   common-only transfer, with shielding/certification as applicable;
1097: - `Fhat` wins while real F is live: terminal-fidelity/carrier failure, not a
1098:   contradiction to `sigma`; and
1099: - a live class exit is not a win and not permission to stop the underlying
1100:   total pure strategy.  It remains an outer coverage obligation.
