legal padding cell second; after the first append S has only five stones, and
at most two cells could complete an S six, so a supported empty padding cell
outside that finite set exists.  The zero-hole case uses two such fillers.
If either prescribed S append wins, the real engine stops with S winning;
otherwise all pre-existing immediate F holes have been blocked.  F may create
new geometry on later placements, so no eventual outcome is inferred. QED.

This is the literal post-event answer.  The coupled shadow history cannot be
continued because its engine is terminal; the real game can continue, but
